# REQUIRES: verilator
# The links' storage kinds, each exact against the target, channels stalled
# or not, and the report's `link kinds` as built:
# - shared links (`--share-links`): the top drives one registered bus to its
#   four lanes, one link for the four model outputs it drives;
# - staged links (`--staged-links`): an early link of one producer instance
#   in two registers, copied at a position of the frame between the reads
#   of consecutive frames (the bus, the lanes' accumulators, the arbiter
#   tree's slices with and without zero-latency links);
# - block and ultra RAM links (`--link-block-depth`, `--link-ultra-depth`):
#   the address units' memories read into the RAM's output register, which
#   is the read register for an input's only source; one of several sources
#   (an address unit's operand from its lane's port) is read a host cycle
#   ahead, then chosen into the read register.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/broadcast
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bc --static --nest --modulo --share-links --compact-links --staged-links Lane 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BC
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/bc/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/bc/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/bc/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/bc/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/bc/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bc0 --static --nest --modulo Lane 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BC0
# BC: shared outputs 5; staged: 11 links, 232 register bits
# BC: link kinds: distributed 0 0 0; block 0 0 0.0; ultra 0 0 0; registers 11 232
# BC0: link storage: 16 memories, 840 bits
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/tree-arb
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/tz --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --staged-links --share-links --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --class-at 'sl@*.slice' --class-at 'root@inner:arb' --class-at 'root@inner:*.join_arb' 'root+Bank' 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TREE
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/tz/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/tz/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/tz/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/tz/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/tz/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +stall=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/t --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --staged-links --class-at 'sl@*.slice' --class-at 'root@inner:arb' --class-at 'root@inner:*.join_arb' 'root+Bank' > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/t/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/t/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/t/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/t/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +stall=30 | FileCheck %s
# TREE: staged 11
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/stateless
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/blk --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --link-block-depth 2 Sm Agu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BLK
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BLKSIM < %t/blk/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/blk/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/blk/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/blk/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/blk/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+6 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/blk/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+7 +stall=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/ult --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --link-ultra-depth 2 Sm Agu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ULT
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/ult/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/ult/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/ult/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/ult/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+8 +stall=30 | FileCheck %s
# Per pair of models (`--link-kinds`): the Sm -> Agu links in ultra RAM, the
# Agu -> Sm ones distributed whatever their depth; the report lists each link.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/lk --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --link-block-depth 2 --link-kinds Sm_model:Agu:ultra,Agu:Sm_model:distributed Sm Agu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LK
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LKUSE < %t/lk/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/lk/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/lk/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/lk/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/lk/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+9 +stall=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: not foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/lkx --static --nest --modulo --link-kinds Sm_model:Nope:block Sm Agu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LKX
# LK: link kinds: distributed {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}}; block 0 0 0.0; ultra [[U:[1-9][0-9]*]]
# LK: block/ultra [[U]]
# LKUSE-NOT: link use Agu Sm_model {{[0-9]+ [0-9]+ [0-9]+}} block
# LKUSE: link use Sm_model Agu {{[0-9]+ [0-9]+ [0-9]+}} ultra 1
# LKX: link-kinds: no class model 'Nope'
# BLK: link kinds: distributed {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}}; block [[N:[1-9][0-9]*]] {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9.]+}}; ultra 0
# BLK: block/ultra [[N]] (read ahead {{[1-9][0-9]*}})
# BLKSIM: seq.firmem 1, 1, old, undefined {sv.attributes = [#sv.attribute<"ram_style" = "\22block\22">]}
# ULT: link kinds: {{.*}}; block 0 0 0.0; ultra [[M:[1-9][0-9]*]]
# ULT: block/ultra [[M]]
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH 196 cycles
